@voice takahashi-wen
// The Commons writer, draft 1 (non-story crew). Comms officer, night. (The roster says "they"; this card does too.)
tpl: brisk
talk: Short and blunt; no small talk, no padding. Calls anything vague "static" ("That's static. Say what you mean."). Practical: answers the question you should have asked. But get them on music and the sentences get longer and warmer. Has gone from listening in the music room to playing.
cares: a clean signal | the record cabinet's songs | calling home | their journal of every star they've seen
jokes: anything vague is "static" | they can tune a signal out of static like picking a lock, and can't tune a guitar to save themselves (they can, they just say so)
hi: Hey | You | Hi
bye: Out | Later | Go on
yes: Yes | Done | Fine
thanks: Thanks | Good
wow: Huh. Clean | Nice
sigh: Static
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: guarded
loves: music
likes: star | tea
invites: music
joy: playing in the music room after the night shift
thread: talent
keepsake: a page from their star journal, the night you were both on watch
avoid: being called shy (they aren't; they just don't waste words)
